<title>PARAGUAY: SOCCER-PARAGUAY BEAT PERU 2-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-PARAGUAY BEAT PERU 2-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>ASUNCION 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Paraguay beat Peru 2-1</p>
<p>(halftime 2-1) in a South American World Cup qualifier on</p>
<p>Wednesday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Paraguay - Catalino Rivarola (12), Aristides Rojas (40)</p>
<p>Peru - Jose Pereda (33)</p>
<p>	 Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost,</p>
<p>goals for, goals against, points)</p>
<p> Colombia     8  5  2  1  14  6 17</p>
<p> Paraguay     8  5  2  1  10  4 17</p>
<p> Argentina    8  3  4  1  11  7 13</p>
<p> Ecuador	8  4  0  4  12  9 12</p>
<p> Uruguay	8  3  1  4   6 10 10</p>
<p> Bolivia	8  2  4  2  12  8 10</p>
<p> Chile	  8  2  3  3  11 12  9</p>
<p> Peru	   8  2  3  3   9 11  9		 </p>
<p> Venezuela    8  0  1  7   5 23  1</p>
<p>Note: top four teams qualify for the 1998 World Cup in</p>
<p>France. Brazil qualify automatically as holders.</p>
</text>
